  "notes": "Flagship tier of GPT-5.6, the first OpenAI family named with the Sol, Terra and Luna tiers (preview post: the number identifies the generation, the tier names identify durable capability tiers). Prominence standard because it is a point version and, per the API docs, continues the unsuffixed GPT-5 tier under a new name; review if the Sol line should count as a new flagship line. The API alias gpt-5.6 routes to this model; GPT-5.6 is also the family name, hence candidate. An updated GPT-5.6 Sol for ChatGPT conversations followed on 2026-08-06 and has its own record (openai.gpt-5-6-sol-2026-08); Codex and ChatGPT Work kept this July version. The openai.com posts were read through Wayback Machine captures because openai.com answers scripted requests with HTTP 403."
